(1777146, 240630, 37875, '<td valign="top">interesting shot of blowing leaves.  when i think "circle of life" i think about birth, death, and rebirth.  imo, title does not match image (light on the birth and rebirth aspects).  what DOES give me cause to celebrate is being able to watch leaves swirling about the sidewalk, though!  <br/>in terms of this pic, beyond the challenge, i love it.  i love the colors and the exposure and the contrast of shapes (grid vs circles vs pavers picking up the grid pattern again). i love the yellow in the leaves, and how that one grid square and leaf towards the center just anchor the eye in the shot.   part of me wonders how this image would look with a wee bit of cropping to center the grid, but most of me really prefers the asymetric layout.  so, mismatched title (and i''m being called on that same thing in this challenge, too), but nicely done, and a groovy photo!</td>', 'interesting shot of blowing leaves.  when i think "circle of life" i think about birth, death, and rebirth.  imo, title does not match image (light on the birth and rebirth aspects).  what DOES give me cause to celebrate is being able to watch leaves swirling about the sidewalk, though!  in terms of this pic, beyond the challenge, i love it.  i love the colors and the exposure and the contrast of shapes (grid vs circles vs pavers picking up the grid pattern again). i love the yellow in the leaves, and how that one grid square and leaf towards the center just anchor the eye in the shot.   part of me wonders how this image would look with a wee bit of cropping to center the grid, but most of me really prefers the asymetric layout.  so, mismatched title (and i''m being called on that same thing in this challenge, too), but nicely done, and a groovy photo!', '2005-10-11 18:20:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(1777147, 242088, 37875, '<td valign="top">nice choice of subject, and beautiful models.  the angle of the shot makes the child''s hand appear disproportionately large.  i would be interested in seeing how a darker background would have affected the richness of this photo.  imo, all the light colors wash away the impact of this tender scene.  for example, even looking at the right side of the shot...the shadowed background makes the child''s head pop out at you more than the light side.  OR...how would this have looked with a dark background and some off-side lighting options, then done as a b&amp;w to really have those sweet faces pop out?</td>', 'nice choice of subject, and beautiful models.  the angle of the shot makes the child''s hand appear disproportionately large.  i would be interested in seeing how a darker background would have affected the richness of this photo.  imo, all the light colors wash away the impact of this tender scene.  for example, even looking at the right side of the shot...the shadowed background makes the child''s head pop out at you more than the light side.  OR...how would this have looked with a dark background and some off-side lighting options, then done as a b&w to really have those sweet faces pop out?', '2005-10-11 18:20:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(1777148, 242236, 37875, '<td valign="top">nice concept.  i like the hanging drop on the orange, and choice of colors.  the interior orange wedge picks up the color of the beverage, which casts an odd hue.  i don''t know if this is the case, but the hanging curls in the background appear to have been edited in?  there''s an odd outline around them that''s distracting.</td>', 'nice concept.  i like the hanging drop on the orange, and choice of colors.  the interior orange wedge picks up the color of the beverage, which casts an odd hue.  i don''t know if this is the case, but the hanging curls in the background appear to have been edited in?  there''s an odd outline around them that''s distracting.', '2005-10-11 18:20:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(1777150, 242038, 37875, '<td valign="top">35 years is certainly something to celebrate!  such a sweet couple, but i wish i could see more of his face.   the image also appears a bit fuzzy in the faces...<br/>i would be interested to see how this picture looks with a darker background and tighter/closer composition to really highlight the love and joy in their faces.</td>', '35 years is certainly something to celebrate!  such a sweet couple, but i wish i could see more of his face.   the image also appears a bit fuzzy in the faces...i would be interested to see how this picture looks with a darker background and tighter/closer composition to really highlight the love and joy in their faces.', '2005-10-11 18:20:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(1777151, 242075, 37875, '<td valign="top">great picture composition and background.  the model''s expression is awesome, and that certainly is a whopper of a pumpkin!  the lighting (particularly in the face) feels a bit overexposed, which washes him out and weakens the photo.  i would love to see this photo edited to tone the brightness down just a bit...it''s such a great shot!</td>', 'great picture composition and background.  the model''s expression is awesome, and that certainly is a whopper of a pumpkin!  the lighting (particularly in the face) feels a bit overexposed, which washes him out and weakens the photo.  i would love to see this photo edited to tone the brightness down just a bit...it''s such a great shot!', '2005-10-11 18:20:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(1777153, 242174, 37875, '<td valign="top">cool shot, with lots of groovy faces and emotions.  it would have been so much more powerful had that guy in the center not looked into the camera when you took it...dang!  you can feel the celebration just looking at this photo, though!  fun, like the graininess to the photo--makes it feel like a newspaper pic.  does the title refer to the size of the audience?</td>', 'cool shot, with lots of groovy faces and emotions.  it would have been so much more powerful had that guy in the center not looked into the camera when you took it...dang!  you can feel the celebration just looking at this photo, though!  fun, like the graininess to the photo--makes it feel like a newspaper pic.  does the title refer to the size of the audience?', '2005-10-11 18:21:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(1777154, 241436, 37875, '<td valign="top">hilarious!  the poor guy had to wait for so long...  ; )<br/>fun photo, nice crop and composition, i would almost like to see sharper b&amp;w in the saturation, to pull out greater detail and definition in the image (e.g. leaves &amp; model''s hair against background) but this is a nice happy fun photo.  hope those sox keep spanking the yanks!</td>', 'hilarious!  the poor guy had to wait for so long...  ; )fun photo, nice crop and composition, i would almost like to see sharper b&w in the saturation, to pull out greater detail and definition in the image (e.g. leaves & model''s hair against background) but this is a nice happy fun photo.  hope those sox keep spanking the yanks!', '2005-10-11 18:21:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(1777155, 241731, 37875, '<td valign="top">the orange looks oversaturated...to the point of being distracting, in my eye.  with the grey sky, i wonder how this picture would have looked as a b&amp;w?</td>', 'the orange looks oversaturated...to the point of being distracting, in my eye.  with the grey sky, i wonder how this picture would have looked as a b&w?', '2005-10-11 18:21:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(1777156, 241007, 37875, '<td valign="top">the pumpkins look ready for watching some football!  : )<br/>i would be interested in seeing how this photo would look with deeper orange tones...the lighting/reflection of the pumpkin skins makes them appear to be a bit washed out.  i also wonder how this shot could be framed to add more energy and visual interest...perhaps taken at an angle to cary the pumpkin line 2/3rds of the way across the image field?</td>', 'the pumpkins look ready for watching some football!  : )i would be interested in seeing how this photo would look with deeper orange tones...the lighting/reflection of the pumpkin skins makes them appear to be a bit washed out.  i also wonder how this shot could be framed to add more energy and visual interest...perhaps taken at an angle to cary the pumpkin line 2/3rds of the way across the image field?', '2005-10-11 18:21:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(1777157, 242093, 37875, '<td valign="top">FUN!  at first i missed the smoke effect and thought the picture was a bit blurry/washed out, but then i got it.  love the action shot of the cigar!  love your model! Fun fun fun!  ; )</td>', 'FUN!  at first i missed the smoke effect and thought the picture was a bit blurry/washed out, but then i got it.  love the action shot of the cigar!  love your model! Fun fun fun!  ; )', '2005-10-11 18:21:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(1777160, 242233, 37875, '<td valign="top">okay, you and i are probably getting faulted for the same thing...the title is what makes the picture qualify for the challenge, and not the picture itself. but hey, that''s life, right?  now for the pic.  i think it''s beautiful.  i like the dof, i love the palate of colors.  i like how the doe''s leg is picked up just a bit, and how she''s looking into the camera.  there''s even light in her eyes, so that''s cool too.  a nicely composed shot that makes me feel happy to know that this doe gets to exist in peace for one more year!</td>', 'okay, you and i are probably getting faulted for the same thing...the title is what makes the picture qualify for the challenge, and not the picture itself. but hey, that''s life, right?  now for the pic.  i think it''s beautiful.  i like the dof, i love the palate of colors.  i like how the doe''s leg is picked up just a bit, and how she''s looking into the camera.  there''s even light in her eyes, so that''s cool too.  a nicely composed shot that makes me feel happy to know that this doe gets to exist in peace for one more year!', '2005-10-11 18:21:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(1777161, 241828, 37875, '<td valign="top">this photo makes me feel happy and content.  great dof.  lovely warm tones in your color treatment.  i want to know who/what your model is smiling at, it draws me in to the picture.  very nicely done!</td>', 'this photo makes me feel happy and content.  great dof.  lovely warm tones in your color treatment.  i want to know who/what your model is smiling at, it draws me in to the picture.  very nicely done!', '2005-10-11 18:21:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(1777163, 241943, 37875, '<td valign="top">LOVE it!  i love that you captured the granddaughter looking into the camera, and grandpa looking so lovingly at her.  great composition, nice b&amp;w tones, nice use of negative space.  this image just warms my heart and makes me happy.  hope you finish really high.</td>', 'LOVE it!  i love that you captured the granddaughter looking into the camera, and grandpa looking so lovingly at her.  great composition, nice b&w tones, nice use of negative space.  this image just warms my heart and makes me happy.  hope you finish really high.', '2005-10-11 18:21:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(1777164, 242067, 37875, '<td valign="top">...and we''re making some money off of those apples, too, at $7/lb!  woah!  : )<br/>it would be interesting to see if adjusting the levels and curves of this image would remove the dark film, allowing the colors to pop more and allowing the viewer to see the detail in the people''s faces.</td>', '...and we''re making some money off of those apples, too, at $7/lb!  woah!  : )it would be interesting to see if adjusting the levels and curves of this image would remove the dark film, allowing the colors to pop more and allowing the viewer to see the detail in the people''s faces.', '2005-10-11 18:22:02.000000', NULL, 1),
