(1801162, 242148, 38267, '<td valign="top">Congrats on capturing such a great image, as well as winning as ribbon.</td>', 'Congrats on capturing such a great image, as well as winning as ribbon.', '2005-10-21 14:02:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(1801234, 242231, 26255, '<td valign="top"><b>**Critique Club**</b> <br/> <br/><b><u>Initial Impression:</u></b> Nice candid!<br/> <br/><b><u>Detailed analysis:</u></b> Personally I think this is a very good shot.  The choice of using black and white was an excellent one.  You''ve done an excellent job of capturing a very good "slice of life" image.  The expressions on the women definitely convey a sense of celebration.  The DOF is perfect.  I think by not showing the entire circle of friends and focusing mainly on one woman, you''ve done a great job of reinforcing the feeling.  My only nitpick is the one lady in the background.  She does distract from the image slightly, but if you had waited for someone to pass in front of her to snap your shot, who knows, you may not have had as powerful an image.  I didn''t vote on this one, but if I did, I would have seen her as a distraction, but an unavoidable one.<br/> <br/><b><u>Overall Impression:</u></b>Brad, you do great work and I''m really not qualified to critique it.  I hope you find this little bit of insight (from an untrained eye) helpful.  <b>GREAT SHOT!!!</b></td>', '**Critique Club**  Initial Impression: Nice candid! Detailed analysis: Personally I think this is a very good shot.  The choice of using black and white was an excellent one.  You''ve done an excellent job of capturing a very good "slice of life" image.  The expressions on the women definitely convey a sense of celebration.  The DOF is perfect.  I think by not showing the entire circle of friends and focusing mainly on one woman, you''ve done a great job of reinforcing the feeling.  My only nitpick is the one lady in the background.  She does distract from the image slightly, but if you had waited for someone to pass in front of her to snap your shot, who knows, you may not have had as powerful an image.  I didn''t vote on this one, but if I did, I would have seen her as a distraction, but an unavoidable one. Overall Impression:Brad, you do great work and I''m really not qualified to critique it.  I hope you find this little bit of insight (from an untrained eye) helpful.  GREAT SHOT!!!', '2005-10-21 14:47:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(1801264, 242231, 19708, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Palmetto_Pixels:</b></div><hr/><i>..... and I''m really not qualified to critique it.  [/b] </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Thanks Lee, I appreciate you taking the time.<br/>I would have never selected a request for a critique, but the score was making me wonder what was wrong with it.<br/><i>(other than not being Photoshopped to daylights)</i> <br/> <br/>Regarding what I quoted you on there, you are so wrong.<br/>We all put our pants on the same way, and are qualified to reflect what<br/>works or doesn''t in an image, and appreciate the honest opinion.<br/></td>', 'Originally posted by Palmetto_Pixels:..... and I''m really not qualified to critique it.  [/b]  Thanks Lee, I appreciate you taking the time.I would have never selected a request for a critique, but the score was making me wonder what was wrong with it.(other than not being Photoshopped to daylights)  Regarding what I quoted you on there, you are so wrong.We all put our pants on the same way, and are qualified to reflect whatworks or doesn''t in an image, and appreciate the honest opinion.', '2005-10-21 15:11:40.000000', NULL, 0),
