(1802512, 241892, 41675, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club. While many chose something bright or fun to celebrate in this challenge, I like how you chose to celebrate something a bit simpler - nature and it''s beauty.<br/> <br/>I agree with many of the voters that you wonderfully captured the fog. Terrific mornign light exposture as well. For me, the water fowl add the bit of needed interest to keep it from being a run of the mill scenic landscape.<br/> <br/>My eyes keep being drawn to the tree in the middle when I look at your image. Sometimes, I personally find that keeping the main subject(s) slightly off-center, it keeps me a bit more interested.<br/> <br/>Overall however, a really terrific shot. One to be proud of.</td>', 'Hello from the critique club. While many chose something bright or fun to celebrate in this challenge, I like how you chose to celebrate something a bit simpler - nature and it''s beauty. I agree with many of the voters that you wonderfully captured the fog. Terrific mornign light exposture as well. For me, the water fowl add the bit of needed interest to keep it from being a run of the mill scenic landscape. My eyes keep being drawn to the tree in the middle when I look at your image. Sometimes, I personally find that keeping the main subject(s) slightly off-center, it keeps me a bit more interested. Overall however, a really terrific shot. One to be proud of.', '2005-10-22 00:19:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(1802521, 241826, 41675, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the critique club.<br/> <br/>I''m happy this photo came up for me to discuss, as it was one of my favorites in the challenge.<br/> <br/>A very nice, and different point of view from the usual wedding photos. Terrific DOF, and the use of sepia gives it a nice, warm feeling for me. You successfully captured a celebration moment that is easily recognizable by any viewer.<br/> <br/>Congratulations on your finish and I look forward to seeing more of your work in the future - you''re quite talented.</td>', 'Greetings from the critique club. I''m happy this photo came up for me to discuss, as it was one of my favorites in the challenge. A very nice, and different point of view from the usual wedding photos. Terrific DOF, and the use of sepia gives it a nice, warm feeling for me. You successfully captured a celebration moment that is easily recognizable by any viewer. Congratulations on your finish and I look forward to seeing more of your work in the future - you''re quite talented.', '2005-10-22 00:24:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(1802529, 239674, 41675, '<td valign="top">Hello and greetings from the Critque Club.<br/> <br/>I think you had a good concept for the challenge. With a few tweaks and adjustments (and a brighter day), I think this shot would improve.<br/> <br/>overall, I would have liked to seen it a bit more in focus. The composition isn''t bad, but I agree with other voters during the challenge that having a bit more room under her boots, and not having them sit on the border would be more effective.<br/> <br/>While the girl herself appears to be celebration, the majority of your photo is a bit on the dark side. Had this been a brighter, sunnier day, I think the message would be even stronger.<br/> <br/>Like I said, you had a good idea - it shows me you have creativity. Keep up the nice work and try different times of the day to see how natural lighting affects your main subject.<br/> <br/>I look forward to seeing you enter future challenges. Thank you.</td>', 'Hello and greetings from the Critque Club. I think you had a good concept for the challenge. With a few tweaks and adjustments (and a brighter day), I think this shot would improve. overall, I would have liked to seen it a bit more in focus. The composition isn''t bad, but I agree with other voters during the challenge that having a bit more room under her boots, and not having them sit on the border would be more effective. While the girl herself appears to be celebration, the majority of your photo is a bit on the dark side. Had this been a brighter, sunnier day, I think the message would be even stronger. Like I said, you had a good idea - it shows me you have creativity. Keep up the nice work and try different times of the day to see how natural lighting affects your main subject. I look forward to seeing you enter future challenges. Thank you.', '2005-10-22 00:31:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(1802773, 242148, 46457, '<td valign="top">it''s a magical moment,nice captured..congratulations</td>', 'it''s a magical moment,nice captured..congratulations', '2005-10-22 08:36:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(1802832, 241731, 29490, '<td valign="top">*A Critique Club Comment*<br/> <br/>Aloha Eric<br/> <br/>Please keep in mind I''m not a trained professional ...<br/> <br/><b>Composition</b> <br/>I like the formation, too bad the trailing jet isn''t a tad higher but you have very little control over that.  I agree with the others who''ve stated more pixels are needed on the right, I think less magnification and a near-pano crop may have been the ticket for this orientation of the jets.<br/> <br/><b>Technical / Post Processing</b> <br/>My feeling is that you pushed the limits of your lens and did what you could PP to bring out the planes.  I may be wrong, only you know, but that is the feeling I get looking at the photo.  The overall color is off (as others have mentioned).  Some selective color editing would really make this photo pop - give the sky a bluer blue, the yellows less orange. The halo is distracting, cloning that out would have helped.<br/> <br/><b>Aesthetics</b> <br/>I do not find the photo aesthetically displeasing, however I find it lacks a pop.<br/> <br/><b>Relevance to Challenge</b> <br/>I find the Blue Angels to be relevant to the challenge.  They might have been a much better fit and more widely accepted in the recent "Pride" challenge.<br/> <br/><b>Overall</b> <br/>Overall I think this is a nice photo that could have scored much higher had you employed a different crop and did some selective color editing.<br/> <br/>I always enjoy seeing your photos and you have quite the excellent portfolio, I look forward to seeing your future work.<br/> <br/>-jp<br/></td>', '*A Critique Club Comment* Aloha Eric Please keep in mind I''m not a trained professional ... Composition I like the formation, too bad the trailing jet isn''t a tad higher but you have very little control over that.  I agree with the others who''ve stated more pixels are needed on the right, I think less magnification and a near-pano crop may have been the ticket for this orientation of the jets. Technical / Post Processing My feeling is that you pushed the limits of your lens and did what you could PP to bring out the planes.  I may be wrong, only you know, but that is the feeling I get looking at the photo.  The overall color is off (as others have mentioned).  Some selective color editing would really make this photo pop - give the sky a bluer blue, the yellows less orange. The halo is distracting, cloning that out would have helped. Aesthetics I do not find the photo aesthetically displeasing, however I find it lacks a pop. Relevance to Challenge I find the Blue Angels to be relevant to the challenge.  They might have been a much better fit and more widely accepted in the recent "Pride" challenge. Overall Overall I think this is a nice photo that could have scored much higher had you employed a different crop and did some selective color editing. I always enjoy seeing your photos and you have quite the excellent portfolio, I look forward to seeing your future work. -jp', '2005-10-22 09:59:39.000000', NULL, 0),
